Replaces document validation test with UI interaction tests for Visa Support page. Previous implementation tested 193 country pages for required visa documents; new implementation tests search, navigation, and pagination controls.

## Changes

### Test Coverage
- **Search box**: Type "Afghanistan", verify single result, clear with reset button
- **Country card navigation**: Click country link, verify page load via URL pattern
- **Pagination**: Click Next button, then jump to last page (max pagination number)
- **Per page dropdown**: Select 50 items, verify display update

### Implementation
- Follows `BlogsTest.java` and `ProgramsFilterTest.java` patterns exactly
- JavaScript clicks throughout to avoid overlay issues
- Same driver init, logging system, screenshot capture, cookie handling
- Base URL: `https://studyleo.com/en`

### Helper Methods
```java
// Extract first number from "Showing 20 of 190" text with bounds checking
private int getShowingCount()

// Find highest numeric pagination link
private int getMaxPageNumber()

// Click reset button via parent element (JavaScript)
private void clickResetButton()
```

### Element Locators
```java
searchBox = "input[data-slot='input'][aria-label='Search Countries']"
resultCounter = "span.text-xs.text-black-text.opacity-80.font-medium"
resetButton = "//button[@data-slot='button']//span[normalize-space(text())='Reset']"
countryCardLocator = "main section ul li a[href*='/visa-support/']"
perPageDropdown = "button[type='button'][aria-labelledby='per-page-options']"
```

## Technical Notes
- Exact match for "50" option to avoid matching "150" or "500"
- Dual URL patterns for country pages: `/visa-support/` and `/study-visa-support-in-turkey/`
- Array bounds checking prevents `ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException` in text parsing
- 543 lines (down from 700), 4 tests vs previous multi-page iteration

