## Objective
Create a new test file `src/test/VisaSupportTest.java` to test the **Visa Support page functionality** on StudyLeo website.

## Test Scenario
1. Open StudyLeo website and navigate to Visa Support page
2. Test search box with "Afghanistan" keyword, verify result shows 1 country, then clear with reset button
3. Click on a country card and verify the page loads successfully (HTTP 200)
4. Navigate back, click Next page button, then click the last page (highest pagination number)
5. Open Per Page dropdown and select 50, verify "50 per page" is displayed

## Important: Follow the same patterns as BlogsTest.java and ProgramsFilterTest.java
- Use the same driver initialization, logging system, and screenshot functionality
- Use the same base URL: `https://studyleo.com/en`
- Use the same cookie accept logic
- Use JavaScript clicks for all interactions (to avoid overlay issues)

## Element Locators

### Navigation
- **Visa Support Link:** `By.cssSelector("a[data-slot='navigation-menu-link'][href='/en/study-visa-support-in-turkey']")`

### Search Box
- **Locator:** `By.cssSelector("input[data-slot='input'][aria-label='Search Countries']")`

### Result Counter
```html
<span class="text-xs md:text-sm text-black-text opacity-80 font-medium">Showing 20 of 190</span>
```
- **Locator:** `By.cssSelector("span.text-xs.text-black-text.opacity-80.font-medium")` or find span containing "Showing"
- Extract the first number: "Showing **20** of 190" → 20
- After searching "Afghanistan", should show "Showing **1** of 190"

### Reset Button (JavaScript click required)
- **Locator:** `By.xpath("//button[@data-slot='button']//span[normalize-space(text())='Reset']")`
- Must click the parent button, not the span

### Country Card
- **Locator:** `By.xpath("/html/body/main/div/section/div/div[2]/ul/li/a[2]")`
- Or more reliable: `By.cssSelector("main section ul li a[href*='/visa-support/']")`

### Pagination Buttons
